  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conference on Sustainable Sourcing in the Garment Sector in Bangladesh (Part B)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conference on Sustainable Sourcing in the Garment Sector of Bangladesh (MAN16BD01).On 29 September 2016, the Sustainable Sourcing in the Garment Sector (SSGS) conference was held in Dhaka, Bangladesh. SSGS convened 380 high-profile participants from over 190 organisations to discuss sustainable versus unsustainable sourcing and showcase new sourcing practices that would benefit all stakeholders in the garment value chain. Amongst the representatives were officials from the Government of Bangladesh and the Netherlands, Corps Diplomatique, NGOs, International Organisations, academics, international buyers, brands and suppliers. The Netherlands Minister for Foreign Trade and Development Cooperation was present for a keynote speech.SSGS emphasised the need to advance a common understanding of sustainable sourcing practices in the garment sector by promoting multi-stakeholder cooperation and presenting best practices. The SSGS conference was a subsequent event to the Asian Living Wage Conference (ALWC) in May 2016. The ALWC was convened through the joint efforts of the governments of Germany, the Netherlands, and Pakistan. The ALWC focused on realising living wages through social dialogue. The SSGS conference highlighted the importance of sustainable sourcing practices for buyers, suppliers, and other stakeholders involved in the garment value chain.</narrative>
  </description>
